index d72c8c7..f8282d3 100644
--- a/docs/business-rules.md
+++ b/docs/business-rules.md
@@ -98,7 +98,35 @@ ### Ticket
 
 **Immutability enforcement:** the write-once rule is enforced on the `Ticket` model (`updating` hook), so it applies to Eloquent saves only — mass updates through the query builder (`Ticket::query()->update(...)`) bypass it and must not be used on issued tickets.
 
-**Single-ticket call (scope note):** `Ticket::call()` marks one waiting ticket as `called` (entity-membership checked, exactly-once). This minimal domain primitive proves the mutable `status`/`called_*` fields. Deterministic call-next selection (priority + age + 3-ticket fairness) is implemented by `App\Actions\CallNextTicket` with the three call-panel modes below (`any` applies fairness; `priority_only`/`normal_only` ignore it); AuthZ stays out of scope per #20 and HTTP/Livewire panels remain future work.
+**Single-ticket call (scope note):** `Ticket::call()` marks one waiting ticket as `called` (exactly-once). This minimal domain primitive proves the mutable `status`/`called_*` fields. Deterministic call-next selection (priority + age + 3-ticket fairness) is implemented by `App\Actions\CallNextTicket` with the three call-panel modes below (`any` applies fairness; `priority_only`/`normal_only` ignore it). Both paths authorize the caller with the queue `call` ability (see [Queue Management and Access](#queue-management-and-access)); HTTP/Livewire panels remain future work.
+
+### Queue Management and Access
+
+Owners and admins manage the queue catalogue of their entity and decide which employees may call tickets on each queue. Authorization is defined once in `App\Policies\QueuePolicy`.
+
+**Queue lifecycle** (owner and admin only):
+
+| Action | Rules |
+| ------ | ----- |
+| **Create** (`App\Actions\CreateQueue`) | Name is trimmed and 1–255 characters. Slug defaults to the slugified name (`Atendimento Geral` → `atendimento-geral`); an explicit slug is slugified too. New queues are active. |
+| **Update** (`App\Actions\UpdateQueue`) | Any combination of name, slug and active flag; omitted (`null`) values are left unchanged. Keeping the queue's own slug is allowed. |
+| **Delete** | **Not supported.** A queue is retired by deactivation (`is_active = false`): its tickets are preserved, and issuing or calling on it fails. |
+
+Slugs are unique **within an entity**; the same slug may exist in another entity. Taking a slug used by another queue of the same entity is a validation error.
+
+**Per-queue access** (`App\Actions\SetQueueAccess`, owner and admin only):
+
+A manager sets the permissions of an entity member on a queue. The only permission today is `call`. A non-empty list grants it; an empty list revokes it. Employees cannot change their own access, and a membership and queue from different entities are rejected.
+
+| Who | May call tickets on the queue? |
+| --- | --- |
+| Owner or admin of the queue's entity | Yes, always (no grant needed) |
+| Employee with a grant for **that** queue whose permissions include `call` | Yes |
+| Any other employee, member of another entity, or non-member | No (`AuthorizationException`) |
+
+Grants and revocations are written to the `audit` log as `queue.access.granted` and `queue.access.revoked` (with `actor_id`, `queue_id` and `entity_membership_id`). Revoking a membership that has no grant is a no-op and is not logged.
+
+**Call authorization:** `CallNextTicket` (every call mode) and `Ticket::call()` check the `call` ability after confirming the queue is active. An inactive queue rejects the call with `InactiveQueueException` before any authorization check.
 
 ### Priority
 
